Package: KNN.normalization
Title: Neighbor-Based Normalization of CITE-Seq Protein Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Javier", "Marchena-Hurtado", , "javier.marchena.hurtado@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: KNN normalization is a normalization method for protein counts in
    CITE-seq data. It learns from neighbor cells in a k-nearest-neighbor (KNN)
    graph in order to estimate the appropriate total protein counts in each
    cell, accurately estimating total protein counts while preserving
    biological information. This package works on 'Seurat' objects and is the
    R counterpart of the Python package 'KNN_normalization', which is based on
    'scanpy'.
